# Mobile-native UI gate (always-on)

Every **UI change** in `ui/src/**` must preserve the **native app** mobile experience from the mobile-native redesign, not a shrunk desktop layout.

## When this applies

- New or changed pages, components, modals, menus, toolbars, forms, cards, tables, empty states
- Layout, spacing, typography, or navigation on any screen
- **Skip:** backend/edge/SQL with no UI; internal renames with no layout/component change

## Before implementing (mandatory)

1. **Load the full spec:** `.cursor/rules/mobile-responsive.mdc` (auto on `ui/src/**` in Cursor) or invoke the **`mobile-responsive`** skill (Claude Code / OpenCode; not auto-loaded there).
2. **Design mobile first** at 375px, then scale with `sm:` / `md:` / `lg:`.
3. **Reuse shared primitives** in `ui/src/components/mobile/` and `ResponsiveModal`. Do not hand-roll fixed bottom bars, hamburger drawers, or centered phone modals.

| Need                            | Use                                                           |
| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Modal / form                    | `ResponsiveModal` (+ `GuestDialogShell` / `AdminDialogShell`) |
| Option list / picker            | `MobileChoiceSheet` + `MobileChoiceItem`                      |
| Overflow ⋯ menu                 | `ResponsiveOverflowMenu` (marketing: `MarketingOverflowMenu`) |
| Bottom nav                      | `BottomTabBar` + `BottomBarSlotProvider`                      |
| Dominant Save / Back / Continue | `ContextualActionBar`                                         |
| Admin page                      | `AdminMobilePage` + `MobileBrandHero`                         |
| List filters on phone           | `AdminListRefineSheet`                                        |
| Hero trailing actions           | `MobileHeroActionMenu` (one ··· max, not a row of icons)      |

## Hard rules below `lg` (`max-lg`)

- **No centered `Dialog`** for forms, pickers, or confirms. Use bottom sheets via `ResponsiveModal`. Exceptions: `AlertDialog`, full-screen media/document lightboxes, full-screen video tour.
- **No floating `DropdownMenu` panels** for option lists or overflow actions. Use `MobileChoiceSheet` / `ResponsiveOverflowMenu`.
- **One bottom nav layer.** Tab bar or `ContextualActionBar`, never both stacked. No second bottom tab bar on `/account/*` (top strip only). No hamburger drawer.
- **Touch targets** ≥ 44×44px. Hero icons may use invisible hit pads (`MobileHeroActionButton`).
- **Tab clearance:** `bottomTabBarOffsetClassName()` on the document scrollport or inner fill-main scrollport (not both wrongly).

## Before claiming UI work done

- [ ] §11 checklist in `mobile-responsive.mdc` / skill (375px + 768px, no horizontal scroll, sheets not dropdowns on phone)
- [ ] Modals and menus open as **bottom sheets** on phone
- [ ] Route guide updated if page UX changed (`route-guides` skill)

Inventory: `docs/workflow/for-testing/mobile-native-redesign.md`.
